<title>TURKEY: Iranian oil minister in Turkey for talks.</title>
<headline>Iranian oil minister in Turkey for talks.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iranian Oil Minister Gholamreza Aghazadeh arrived in Turkey on Monday for talks on energy and other areas of cooperation between the two neighbouring countries, state Anatolian news agency said.</p>
<p>It said Aghazadeh's plane was diverted to Istanbul after fog in Ankara airport, where it was originally scheduled to land.</p>
<p>Aghazadeh is expected to meet Turkish President Suleyman Demirel and Energy Minister Recai Kutan.</p>
<p>Iran and Turkey struck a 23-year, $23-billion natural gas agreement in August under which Turkey would buy gas from a pipeline to be built from Tabriz to Ankara.</p>
<p>The agency said a bilateral energy cooperation protocol was expected to be signed during Aghazadeh's visit, which will end on Wednesday</p>
